# Service layer conventions

Services live in `src/services/<domain>/<domain>.service.ts`. They contain all business logic and database access.

## File structure per domain

```
src/services/<domain>/
  <domain>.service.ts   — business logic functions
  <domain>.types.ts     — TypeScript input/output interfaces
```

## Pagination (always use the util)

```typescript
import { getPaginationParams, formatPaginatedResponse, PaginatedResponse } from '../../utils/pagination.util';

async function get<Domain>s(page?: number, limit?: number): Promise<PaginatedResponse<<Domain>Response>> {
  const { page: p, limit: l, skip } = getPaginationParams(page, limit);
  const total = await <Domain>Model.countDocuments(query);
  const items = await <Domain>Model.find(query).skip(skip).limit(l).lean();
  return formatPaginatedResponse(map<Domain>s(items), total, p, l);
}
```

Never hand-roll `skip = (page - 1) * limit` — use `getPaginationParams`.

## Error throwing

Always throw typed errors from `../../types/errors`:

```typescript
import { NotFoundError, ConflictError, ForbiddenError } from '../../types/errors';
import { <DOMAIN>_CODES } from '../../types/codes';

throw new NotFoundError('<Domain> not found', <DOMAIN>_CODES.ERROR_<DOMAIN>_NOT_FOUND);
throw new ForbiddenError('Not authorized', <DOMAIN>_CODES.ERROR_<DOMAIN>_FORBIDDEN);
throw new ConflictError('Already exists', <DOMAIN>_CODES.ERROR_<DOMAIN>_DUPLICATE);
```

Never throw `new Error(...)` — the global error handler doesn't map it properly.

## Mongoose read queries

Always use `.lean()` on read-only queries:
```typescript
const doc = await Model.findById(id).lean();
const docs = await Model.find(query).sort({ date: -1 }).skip(skip).limit(limit).lean();
```

Use `.select('field1 field2')` to project only needed fields.

## Partial updates

Do not build update objects with per-field `if (field !== undefined)` guards. Pass the filtered object directly to `$set`:

```typescript
const updated = await Model.findByIdAndUpdate(
  id,
  { $set: input },          // input already has undefined fields filtered out
  { new: true, runValidators: true }
).lean();
```

## Logging

```typescript
import { logger } from '../../config/logger';
logger.info('Event created', { eventId: event._id, userId });
logger.warn('Payment failed', { paymentId, reason });
```

Never use `console.log`.

## Do not

- Use `any` — `@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any: error` is active. Use explicit types or generics.

## Quality gate

After every change: `npm run pre-commit` must exit with zero TypeScript errors, lint errors, and formatting issues.
